    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for rubygem-mysql2, module.rubygem-mysql2, module.rubygem-bundler, module.rubygem-bson, rubygem-bundler, rubygem-abrt, rubygem-pg, module.rubygem-pg, module.rubygem-abrt, rubygem-bson.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Ruby is an extensible, interpreted, object-oriented, scripting language. It has features to process text files and to perform system management tasks.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* resolv: resolv gem: Denial of Service via uncontrolled memory growth from crafted DNS responses (CVE-2026-80212)\n\n* rubygem-mongo: MongoDB Ruby Driver: Data disclosure and denial of service via query-operator injection (CVE-2026-88030)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
